    statement: "Every note, decision, arc, question and role is written through storytree's write tools: there is one copy, in the library.",
    rule: "Write library content through storytree's tools (write_note, correct_note, the plan tools, raise_question and the rest). Never keep a second copy of knowledge that belongs in the library: a committed mirror, a loose notes file, a document restating a rule. Durable knowledge is a typed note, and other files link to it. Two sessions editing different records never clash; two editing the same field are last-write-wins, so read the current text first and build on it.",
    enforcedBy: "The library's own write refusals: every write is validated at its boundary.",
    failureMode: "Knowledge forks: a copy disagrees with the library, readers cannot tell which is true, and one session's edit silently undoes another's.",
